infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two independent clocks per cache entry
  desc Conflating them is the number-one TanStack Query mistake
  compares
    - label staleTime
      children
        - label Gates refetching
          desc Is data fresh enough to serve without asking the server again?
        - label Default 0
          desc Everything stale at once, so every mount and focus refetches
        - label Trigger-driven
          desc Stale data shown instantly; background refetch on next mount, focus, or reconnect
        - label Too high serves wrong data
          desc A price or permission that lies for minutes
        - label Tune per resource
          desc 0 for a stock price, 30s for a todo list, 10min for a country list
    - label gcTime
      children
        - label Gates memory
          desc After the last subscriber unmounts, how long to keep the entry?
        - label Default 5 min
          desc Inactive entries linger so back-navigation is an instant hit
        - label Unmount-driven
          desc Active entries never collected; the timer starts only at unmount
        - label Too high holds dead data
          desc Stale bytes stay resident, which matters with large lists
        - label Below staleTime defeats it
          desc Entry evicted before its freshness ever helps a returning visitor
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
